   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ עָבַר מִכְּנֶגֶד פָּנָיו, רַבִּי מֵאִיר אוֹמֵר: לֹא יִשְׁתֶּה, וְרַבִּי יוֹסֵי אוֹמֵר: יִשְׁתֶּה.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» In a case where a slave took a vow of naziriteship but was prevented by his master from fulfilling the terms of his vow, the Sages engaged in a dispute what the halakha would be if he permanently «left his» master’s «presence,» i.e., he ran away without being emancipated. «Rabbi Meir says: He may not drink» wine. Since the slave is free in practice, his vow goes into effect. «And Rabbi Yosei says: He may drink» wine, as he is not emancipated."
  }
 ],
